1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,360
A strawberry plant can send out a runner

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,120
that becomes another plant.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:09,400
A flowering plant can also provide both reproductive

4
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,720
cells that join in self-fertilisation.

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,160
Those cells are gametes: a sperm cell and

6
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,040
an egg cell.

7
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:18,040
Joining them is fusion.

8
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:21,080
One plant can be involved in either case,

9
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,440
but the mechanisms differ.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,560
The runner makes a new plant without fusion,

11
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:27,320
so that event is asexual.

12
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:31,560
Self-fertilisation includes fusion, so it is sexual.

13
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,680
Ask what happened, rather than counting the plants

14
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:35,560
we can see.

15
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:40,206
First locate the parts needed for that sexual

16
00:00:40,287 --> 00:00:40,926
pathway.

17
00:00:41,407 --> 00:00:43,006
The anther makes pollen.

18
00:00:43,407 --> 00:00:46,126
The stigma is the surface that receives pollen.

19
00:00:46,607 --> 00:00:48,766
A pollen grain is not just a sperm

20
00:00:48,847 --> 00:00:49,246
cell.

21
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:51,886
It is a small structure that produces or

22
00:00:52,047 --> 00:00:53,406
carries sperm cells.

23
00:00:53,727 --> 00:00:54,926
They have different jobs.

24
00:00:55,647 --> 00:00:57,966
Now follow the route towards the egg.

25
00:00:58,207 --> 00:01:00,526
The style lies between the stigma and the

26
00:01:00,687 --> 00:01:01,166
ovary.

27
00:01:01,567 --> 00:01:03,566
The ovary contains ovules.

28
00:01:04,047 --> 00:01:06,926
Inside an ovule is an embryo sac, containing

29
00:01:07,007 --> 00:01:07,966
the egg cell.

30
00:01:08,207 --> 00:01:12,526
Think of those as nested locations: ovary, ovule,

31
00:01:12,647 --> 00:01:14,366
then the egg's location inside.

32
00:01:14,927 --> 00:01:17,246
Pollen at the stigma is still some distance

33
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:17,966
from the egg.

34
00:01:18,367 --> 00:01:20,366
Arriving there is not the same as a

35
00:01:20,447 --> 00:01:22,766
sperm cell reaching and joining the egg.

36
00:01:24,767 --> 00:01:28,126
Pollination means transferring pollen from an anther to

37
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:29,086
a stigma.

38
00:01:29,407 --> 00:01:32,606
In our example the pollen is compatible, meaning

39
00:01:32,687 --> 00:01:35,006
it can take part in fertilisation with this

40
00:01:35,127 --> 00:01:36,326
receiving plant.

41
00:01:36,607 --> 00:01:39,566
The pollen grain begins growing a pollen tube.

42
00:01:39,807 --> 00:01:42,766
That is pollen germination; it is not a

43
00:01:42,847 --> 00:01:44,806
new plant sprouting from a seed.

44
00:01:45,087 --> 00:01:47,406
The tube grows through the style towards an

45
00:01:47,487 --> 00:01:49,966
ovule and provides a route for sperm cells

46
00:01:50,047 --> 00:01:51,646
to reach the embryo sac.

47
00:01:51,887 --> 00:01:54,486
A sperm cell then joins the egg cell.

48
00:01:54,767 --> 00:01:57,646
Their fusion forms a zygote, the new cell

49
00:01:57,727 --> 00:01:59,526
from which the embryo develops.

50
00:01:59,807 --> 00:02:01,726
This is fertilisation.

51
00:02:02,047 --> 00:02:05,486
So there are three different steps: pollen arrives,

52
00:02:05,567 --> 00:02:08,366
a tube delivers sperm, and sperm joins the

53
00:02:08,527 --> 00:02:09,126
egg.

54
00:02:09,487 --> 00:02:12,446
Reaching the stigma proves pollination, but it does

55
00:02:12,607 --> 00:02:14,766
not prove the later steps succeeded.

56
00:02:16,767 --> 00:02:19,886
After that fusion, the zygote divides and develops

57
00:02:19,967 --> 00:02:23,406
into an embryo, a young developing plant.

58
00:02:23,727 --> 00:02:26,606
The surrounding ovule develops into a seed.

59
00:02:26,927 --> 00:02:29,726
The seed contains the embryo, a protective coat

60
00:02:29,967 --> 00:02:32,446
and stored resources for early growth.

61
00:02:32,767 --> 00:02:35,406
The embryo is inside the seed; it is

62
00:02:35,567 --> 00:02:36,846
not the whole seed.

63
00:02:37,487 --> 00:02:40,206
The ovary usually develops into the fruit around

64
00:02:40,287 --> 00:02:40,926
the seeds.

65
00:02:41,567 --> 00:02:43,886
We are following the embryo-forming part of this

66
00:02:44,087 --> 00:02:47,246
sexual pathway, not every event in the flowering-plant

67
00:02:47,327 --> 00:02:48,046
life cycle.

68
00:02:48,527 --> 00:02:50,766
And a seed forming does not guarantee that

69
00:02:50,807 --> 00:02:52,606
a new plant will become established.

70
00:02:53,007 --> 00:02:55,406
Its later growing conditions still matter.

71
00:02:57,434 --> 00:03:00,073
A strawberry runner is a stem extending from

72
00:03:00,114 --> 00:03:01,353
the parent plant.

73
00:03:01,674 --> 00:03:03,673
A node is a point on the stem

74
00:03:03,754 --> 00:03:05,873
where a leaf or bud arises.

75
00:03:06,154 --> 00:03:08,713
At a suitable node, roots and a shoot

76
00:03:08,794 --> 00:03:10,793
can develop into a new plant.

77
00:03:11,114 --> 00:03:13,193
Cells divide to build that plant.

78
00:03:13,834 --> 00:03:16,473
Mitosis is the division of the nucleus, the

79
00:03:16,554 --> 00:03:18,393
part of the cell containing most of its

80
00:03:18,474 --> 00:03:19,353
DNA.

81
00:03:19,674 --> 00:03:22,073
That builds the new plant without sperm and

82
00:03:22,154 --> 00:03:22,953
egg joining.

83
00:03:23,434 --> 00:03:26,793
This is vegetative propagation: making a new plant

84
00:03:26,874 --> 00:03:29,113
from a part such as a stem, rather

85
00:03:29,194 --> 00:03:30,553
than from gamete fusion.

86
00:03:30,954 --> 00:03:33,273
It is a form of asexual reproduction.

87
00:03:33,754 --> 00:03:36,473
The new plant usually retains the parent's inherited

88
00:03:36,554 --> 00:03:40,313
combination, although mutations can introduce differences.

89
00:03:40,634 --> 00:03:42,793
The runner is not just lengthening the old

90
00:03:42,874 --> 00:03:43,753
plant.

91
00:03:43,834 --> 00:03:46,793
A new rooted plant can become independent, when

92
00:03:47,114 --> 00:03:49,033
resources and conditions support it.

93
00:03:51,034 --> 00:03:54,793
Self-pollination means pollen reaches the same flower, or

94
00:03:54,874 --> 00:03:57,353
another flower on the same plant.

95
00:03:57,514 --> 00:04:01,593
Cross-pollination means pollen travels between different plants.

96
00:04:01,714 --> 00:04:03,673
These names tell us where the pollen came

97
00:04:03,754 --> 00:04:05,513
from and where it went.

98
00:04:05,594 --> 00:04:07,673
They do not by themselves tell us that

99
00:04:07,714 --> 00:04:09,593
fertilisation happened.

100
00:04:09,714 --> 00:04:12,313
When compatible pollen leads to sperm joining an

101
00:04:12,394 --> 00:04:15,993
egg, either route can lead to sexual reproduction.

102
00:04:16,074 --> 00:04:18,713
Our self-compatible plant can use its own pollen

103
00:04:18,754 --> 00:04:20,153
in that pathway.

104
00:04:20,234 --> 00:04:23,033
One plant supplying both gametes does not make

105
00:04:23,234 --> 00:04:25,833
fusion asexual, and it does not guarantee a

106
00:04:25,914 --> 00:04:27,993
genetic copy of that plant.

107
00:04:28,114 --> 00:04:32,553
Cross-fertilisation can combine inherited information from different plants,

108
00:04:32,674 --> 00:04:35,353
but pollen arriving from another plant still does

109
00:04:35,434 --> 00:04:38,313
not guarantee a seed or a surviving offspring.

110
00:04:40,334 --> 00:04:43,133
Apply the fusion question to one supplied case

111
00:04:43,174 --> 00:04:44,333
at a time.

112
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:47,333
First, a strawberry runner develops roots and a

113
00:04:47,374 --> 00:04:48,253
shoot.

114
00:04:48,334 --> 00:04:51,533
The prompt confirms there is no gamete fusion.

115
00:04:51,614 --> 00:04:53,933
A new plant develops from the stem, so

116
00:04:54,014 --> 00:04:57,693
that event is asexual vegetative propagation.

117
00:04:57,934 --> 00:05:02,013
Second, a self-compatible flowering plant supplies both gametes,

118
00:05:02,094 --> 00:05:05,053
and the prompt confirms that sperm joins egg.

119
00:05:05,134 --> 00:05:08,413
Fusion occurs, so that event is sexual even

120
00:05:08,534 --> 00:05:11,213
though both gametes came from one plant.

121
00:05:11,414 --> 00:05:14,173
Third, pollen comes from a different plant, and

122
00:05:14,254 --> 00:05:16,893
sperm-egg fusion is again confirmed.

123
00:05:16,934 --> 00:05:19,613
Fusion makes this event sexual too.

124
00:05:19,654 --> 00:05:22,893
The decisive evidence is the reproductive mechanism.

125
00:05:22,934 --> 00:05:25,693
A count of visible plants, or a pollen-transfer

126
00:05:25,774 --> 00:05:28,813
arrow alone, cannot replace that evidence.

127
00:05:30,834 --> 00:05:34,353
Suppose pollen transfer becomes limited, but the conditions

128
00:05:34,514 --> 00:05:37,073
around a strawberry runner still allow new roots

129
00:05:37,154 --> 00:05:38,513
and shoots to grow.

130
00:05:38,834 --> 00:05:40,913
The runner can make a new plant without

131
00:05:40,994 --> 00:05:41,953
pollen transfer.

132
00:05:42,514 --> 00:05:45,633
It still needs suitable resources and growing conditions.

133
00:05:46,354 --> 00:05:49,553
The sexual pathway can combine inherited information through

134
00:05:49,634 --> 00:05:53,393
gametes, but pollen transfer, sperm delivery and fusion

135
00:05:53,714 --> 00:05:55,073
all need to succeed.

136
00:05:55,714 --> 00:05:58,753
These routes have different opportunities and constraints.

137
00:05:59,074 --> 00:06:01,793
Neither promises that the resulting plant will survive

138
00:06:01,834 --> 00:06:02,913
and reproduce.

139
00:06:04,934 --> 00:06:06,453
Try a supplied model.

140
00:06:07,094 --> 00:06:10,293
Two groups receive compatible pollen on their stigmas.

141
00:06:10,534 --> 00:06:13,333
The pollen is viable, meaning it can germinate

142
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:15,053
under suitable conditions.

143
00:06:15,334 --> 00:06:18,133
In the second group, all pollen tubes stop

144
00:06:18,334 --> 00:06:19,733
before reaching the ovules.

145
00:06:20,214 --> 00:06:22,453
The eggs have not been fertilised, and there

146
00:06:22,534 --> 00:06:23,973
is no other pollen route.

147
00:06:24,614 --> 00:06:27,413
In this model, making a new embryo requires

148
00:06:27,494 --> 00:06:28,853
sperm-egg fusion.

149
00:06:29,414 --> 00:06:31,653
Has pollination occurred in the second group?

150
00:06:32,054 --> 00:06:35,013
Will fertilisation and a new embryo follow through

151
00:06:35,094 --> 00:06:35,813
this pathway?

152
00:06:36,454 --> 00:06:39,173
Explain using the interrupted delivery step.

153
00:06:39,654 --> 00:06:41,413
Pause here to work it through.

154
00:06:53,434 --> 00:06:56,913
Pollination has happened: pollen reached the stigma.

155
00:06:57,194 --> 00:06:59,753
But the tubes stop before delivering sperm to

156
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:01,193
the eggs in this model.

157
00:07:01,434 --> 00:07:04,153
Without that delivery, sperm and egg do not

158
00:07:04,234 --> 00:07:05,433
fuse through this route.

159
00:07:05,834 --> 00:07:08,873
No zygote forms, so no new embryo develops

160
00:07:08,954 --> 00:07:09,513
through it.

161
00:07:09,754 --> 00:07:13,033
Pollen arriving completes the transfer step, not the

162
00:07:13,114 --> 00:07:14,393
later fusion step.

163
00:07:14,794 --> 00:07:17,193
The model also gives no basis for counting

164
00:07:17,314 --> 00:07:18,553
surviving plants.

165
00:07:20,567 --> 00:07:23,366
Classify reproduction by what happens.

166
00:07:23,607 --> 00:07:27,286
In our sexual flowering-plant example, pollen transfer is

167
00:07:27,367 --> 00:07:31,046
followed by sperm delivery, fusion and embryo development.

168
00:07:31,527 --> 00:07:34,166
The ovule develops into a seed containing that

169
00:07:34,247 --> 00:07:34,806
embryo.

170
00:07:35,287 --> 00:07:37,766
A strawberry runner makes a new plant without

171
00:07:37,847 --> 00:07:38,966
gamete fusion.

172
00:07:39,287 --> 00:07:44,006
Self-pollination and cross-pollination describe pollen transfer; neither

173
00:07:44,087 --> 00:07:45,286
is fusion itself.

174
00:07:45,847 --> 00:07:48,326
Producing a new plant also differs from that

175
00:07:48,407 --> 00:07:50,726
plant surviving and reproducing.

176
00:07:51,047 --> 00:07:54,806
The next contributions compare reproduction in fungi, bacteria

177
00:07:54,967 --> 00:07:56,006
and protists.
